// _GLIBCXX_PRECONDITION_ASSERTIONS opts a further step beyond
// _GLIBCXX_CONVEYOR_ASSERTIONS: the library's own conveyor-routed asserts
// (see __glibcxx_assert/__glibcxx_assert_msg below) become genuine declared
// preconditions (pre<>()) on the function's own declaration, with the
// in-body assert disabled, rather than an assertion_STMT inside the body --
// letting the static prover reason about ordinary caller code, not just
// verify the library's own body. Nested under _GLIBCXX_CONVEYOR_ASSERTIONS,
// not an independent mode: a declared precondition here is only ever
// meaningful once its own accessor (e.g. size()) is conveyor-tagged in the
// first place -- so this has no effect at all unless conveyor-assertions
// mode is also active. pre<>()'s own control object here is plain std::
// contracts::conveyor_assert_v, deliberately *not* the std::contracts::
// never_proven_conveyor_v __glibcxx_assert itself routes through below:
// a declared precondition is meant to stay checkable at its own call
// sites (never_proven only ever exempts a mid-body contract_assert's own
// "check against ambient facts" step, which a precondition doesn't go
// through anyway, but using the same never_proven-tagged object here
// regardless would blur that intent). A single #undef here, rather than
// repeating "&& defined(_GLIBCXX_CONVEYOR_ASSERTIONS)" at every
// downstream use of this macro (bits/version.h's own contract-assert
// routing below, debug/assertions.h's own three shared macros, every
// library header this gradually rolls out to -- see _GLIBCXX_
// PRECONDITION_SUBSCRIPT and friends further below for the first three,
// "Stage P1" of that rollout).
#if defined(_GLIBCXX_PRECONDITION_ASSERTIONS) && !defined(_GLIBCXX_CONVEYOR_ASSERTIONS)
# undef _GLIBCXX_PRECONDITION_ASSERTIONS
#endif

